{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport math\n\ndef get_ints():\n    return [int(x) for x in input().split()]\n\ndef safe_add(a, b):\n    return (a + b) % mod\n\ndef safe_mul(a, b):\n    return (a * b) % mod\n\nn, mod = get_ints()\nvalues = [0, 1]\nprefix_sum = 1\n\nfor current in range(2, n + 1):\n    root = int(math.sqrt(current)) + 1\n    accumulator = prefix_sum\n\n    for factor in range(2, root):\n        accumulator = safe_add(accumulator, values[current // factor])\n\n    right = current\n    for index in range(1, current // root + 1):\n        left = current // (index + 1)\n        accumulator = safe_add(accumulator, safe_mul(right - left, values[index]))\n        right = left\n\n    prefix_sum = safe_add(prefix_sum, accumulator)\n    values.append(accumulator)\n\nprint(values[-1])\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<int> get_ints() {\n    string line;\n    getline(cin, line);\n    vector<int> result;\n    int value;\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < line.size(); ) {\n        while (i < line.size() && line[i] == ' ') i++;\n        if (i >= line.size()) break;\n        size_t j = i;\n        while (j < line.size() && line[j] != ' ') j++;\n        result.push_back(stoi(line.substr(i, j - i)));\n        i = j;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint mod;\n\nint safe_add(int a, int b) {\n    return (a + b) % mod;\n}\n\nint safe_mul(int a, int b) {\n    return (a * b) % mod;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    vector<int> input = get_ints();\n    int n = input[0];\n    mod = input[1];\n    \n    vector<int> values;\n    values.push_back(0);\n    values.push_back(1);\n    int prefix_sum = 1;\n    \n    for (int current = 2; current <= n; current++) {\n        int root = (int)sqrt(current) + 1;\n        int accumulator = prefix_sum;\n        \n        for (int factor = 2; factor < root; factor++) {\n            accumulator = safe_add(accumulator, values[current / factor]);\n        }\n        \n        int right = current;\n        for (int index = 1; index <= current / root; index++) {\n            int left = current / (index + 1);\n            accumulator = safe_add(accumulator, safe_mul(right - left, values[index]));\n            right = left;\n        }\n        \n        prefix_sum = safe_add(prefix_sum, accumulator);\n        values.push_back(accumulator);\n    }\n    \n    cout << values.back() << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.67805938469246e-05, -4.768360213347478e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.007967749610543e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.684815212385729e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0011950739426538348, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.396077979938127e-05, -0.5231261253356934, -0.02164829708635807, -1.7165990357170813e-05, -4.768360213347478e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.052396103739738464, -0.016035